---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Criterion lookup"
   summary="Use the wcag command family to find criteria by ID, level, or keyword. Lookup gives you criterion details, coverage status, and testing strategy before you start testing."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>Commands</h2>
      <pre><code>a1 wcag levels --json
a1 wcag criteria --level AA --json
a1 wcag show 4.1.3 --json
a1 wcag search "status message" --json
a1 wcag coverage 4.1.3 --json</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>What lookup returns</h2>
      <ul>
         <li>Criterion ID, title, and conformance level</li>
         <li>Coverage status with linked ACT and axe rule mappings where available</li>
         <li>The testing strategy the runtime can support (automated, hybrid, or manual)</li>
         <li>Structured criterion text so you don't need to look up the W3C spec separately</li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>When to use each command</h2>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><code>wcag levels</code><span>List the conformance levels available for the selected WCAG version.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>wcag criteria --level AA</code><span>List all criteria that belong to a specific level.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>wcag show 4.1.3</code><span>Get full details for one criterion by ID.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>wcag search "status message"</code><span>Find a criterion by keyword when you don't know the exact ID.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>wcag coverage 4.1.3</code><span>Check whether the runtime can test this criterion automatically, with human help, or only manually.</span></div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>Best practice</h2>
      <p>
         Look up the criterion by ID when you can. Use search for discovery when you know the concept
         but not the number. Always check coverage before expecting automated results.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
